{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes of each lottery, defined as the outcome with the minimum probability in each respective lottery. For Lottery A, the least probable outcome is 2400 Euros with a probability of 34%. For Lottery B, the least probable outcome is 2500 Euros with a probability of 33%. Although 33% is slightly lower than 34%, both are the smallest probabilities in their respective lotteries. The reason compares these least probable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., higher monetary value) of these two outcomes. Since 2500 Euros > 2400 Euros, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B. Thus, the decision reason is applicable to the decision problem, and its rule yields a preference for Lottery B.",
